{"book":19,"chapter":100,"context":{"chapter":100,"title":"Enter His Gates with Thanksgiving","summary":"All lands are invited to serve the LORD with gladness and enter his courts with thanks, because he made us, we are his flock, and his goodness and faithfulness last forever.","background":"Title: 'A Psalm of praise,' literally 'for thanksgiving,' possibly sung with the thank offering (Leviticus 7:12). In verse 3 the Hebrew has two readings: 'and not we ourselves' (KJV) or 'and we are his.' The hymn 'All People That on Earth Do Dwell' (the 'Old Hundredth') paraphrases it.","customs":[],"watchFor":["Seven commands: make noise, serve, come, know, enter, be thankful, bless (vv. 1–4).","The reason in verse 5: good, merciful, true."],"connections":["Leviticus 7:12","Psalms 95:7","Ezekiel 34:31","Psalms 117:2"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["מִזְמוֹר","mizmor","H4210","HNcmsa","a psalm"],["לְתוֹדָה","letodah","H8426","HR/Ncfsa","for thanksgiving"]]},"1":{"w":[["הָרִיעוּ","hari'u","H7321","HVhv2mp","shout for joy"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","O all"],["הָאָרֶץ","ha'aretz","H776","HTd/Ncfsa","the earth"]],"x":[[19098004,19098004,43],[42019037,42019037,25],[36003014,36003014,20],[19032011,19032011,19],[19095001,19095002,19],[45015010,45015010,15],[23042010,23042012,14],[19066001,19066001,11],[19117001,19117002,11],[19067004,19067004,9]],"xn":18},"2":{"w":[["עִבְדוּ","'ivdu","H5647","HVqv2mp","serve"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["בְּשִׂמְחָה","besimchah","H8057","HR/Ncfsa","with joy"],["בֹּאוּ","bo'u","H935","HVqv2mp","come"],["לְפָנָיו","lefanav","H6440","HR/Ncmpc/Sp3ms","<to> before him"],["בִּרְנָנָה","birnanah","H7445","HR/Ncfsa","with cries of joy"]],"x":[[50004004,50004004,47],[19095002,19095002,24],[19071023,19071023,21],[5028047,5028047,18],[14020027,14020028,18],[44002046,44002047,18],[19107021,19107022,17],[19042004,19042004,15],[5012012,5012012,12],[5016011,5016